able=\"on\" display=\"block\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">I</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi></mrow><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace></mstyle><mtext>with </mtext><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">O</mi></mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> An M-matrix that is <strong>invertible</strong> is a\n<strong>nonsingular M-matrix</strong>.</p>","file":"ch19-nonnegative/09-m-matrices.html"}